   "text": "Skip to Content\nConnecticut's Official\nState Website\nSearch Bar for CT.gov\nSearch\nLanguage + Settings\nCT.gov Home\nDepartment of Energy & Environmental Protection\nState Parks\nCurrent:\nMassacoe State Forest\nMassacoe State Forest\nWelcome\nOverview/History\nActivities\nFacilities\nFees\nMaps\nGetting Here\nRelated Information\nIn the Area\nContact the Forest\nProvided by:\nDepartment of Energy & Environmental Protection\nWelcome\nMassacoe State Forest\nSimsbury\nMassacoe State Forest consists of two separate blocks of woodland in Simsbury that combine to total 370 acres. The largest block, Great Pond, is home to the town’s biggest standing water body, while the 73 acre Massacoe block adjoins Stratton Brook State Park and provides diverse recreational opportunities.\nContent last updated September 2025\nPolicies\nAccessibility\nAbout CT\nDirectories\nSocial Media\nFor State Employees\nUnited States\nFULL\nConnecticut\nFULL\n© 2026 CT.gov | Connecticut's Official State Website",
