   "final_url": "https://stateparks.utah.gov/parks/camp-floyd/",
   "title": "Camp Floyd State Park Museum | Utah State Parks",
   "text": "Skip to main content\nAn official website of the state of Utah.\nHere is how you know\nOfficial Utah websites use utah.gov in the browser's address bar.\nA Utah.gov website belongs to an official government organization in the state of Utah.\nBe careful when sharing sensitive information.\nShare sensitive information only on secure official Utah.gov websites.\nAn official website of the state of Utah\n© state of Utah\nNotifications\n1\nNotifications\nNotifications\nUtahID Sign In\nUtahID Profile\n, opens in a new tab\nSign Out\nVisit\nFind a Park\nPark Passes\nEvents Calendar\nActivities\nAdventure on Land\nWater Activities\nJr. Ranger Program\nMuseums and Heritage Areas\nDark Skies\nPark Rules & FAQs\nReserve\nExplore\nAbout Us\nNews\nResponsible Recreation\nResponsible Recreation Overview\nFire Safety\nWater Safety\nHeat Safety\nBoat Ramp Conditions\nCold Weather Safety\nMultimedia Library\nJoin Us\nJobs\nJobs Overview\nSeasonal and Part-time Jobs\nVolunteer\nCamp Hosts\nPark Vendors\nResources\nResources Overview\nContact\nAccessibility\nGRAMA Requests\nPrivacy Notice\nVisitation Data\nsearch\nSearch\nSkip to content\nCamp Floyd State Park Museum\nFollow this park\nFacebook\nInstagram\nThe United States Army, Mormon Pioneers, Stagecoach Travelers and the Pony Express met at Camp Floyd and the town of Fairfield. The Army arrived in 1858 and constructed Camp Floyd to suppress a supposed Mormon rebellion. The Army remained here for three years before being recalled for the Civil War. Today, Camp Floyd State Park features three structures and a cemetery. Visit the museum and Stagecoach Inn and learn about this nationally important historic site.\n55°F\nL: 52° H: 58°\nFeels Like 53° Overcast Clouds\nWind: 5 mph SE\nAir Quality: Moderate\nView more park conditions\nHours: Monday – Saturday 9 a.m.-5 p.m.\nHoliday Closures: Thanksgiving, Christmas and New Years Day\nPhone: 801-768-8932\nManagement\nPark Manager: Clay Shelley\nReserve\nDay Pass\nDirections\nActivities\nBiking\nGeocache\nHeritage Area\nJR. Ranger\nMuseum\nAmenities\nGift Shop\nRentable Venues\nRestaurant\nRestrooms\nVisitor Center\nPark Gallery\nMap\nFor a high contrast map, click the green icon in the top right of the map and choose 'Grayscale Enhanced Contrast Map.'\nCamp Floyd State Park Museum | Explore Utah\nOfficial Documentary | Camp Floyd - Forgotten City In The Desert\nEvents\nNotice\nThere are no upcoming events.\nDownloads\nCamp Floyd State Park Museum Brochure\nFees and Features\nCamp Floyd State Park Museum\nHistory\nSchool Field Trips\nPark Fees\nCurrent Conditions\nYouth History Camps\nView All Parks\nFollow us online\nFacebook\n(opens in a new tab)\nX/Twitter\n(opens in a new tab)\nInstagram\n(opens in a new tab)\n1594 West North Temple\nSalt Lake City, UT 84116\nHours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm\nPhone: 801-538-7220\nNavigation Menu\nVisit\nReserve\nExplore\nJoin Us\nResources\nClose search modal\nEnter your search terms\nSearch Now\nend of search form\nAn official website of the state of Utah\n© state of Utah\nUtah.gov Home\n, opens in a new tab\nTerms of Use\n, opens in a new tab\nPrivacy Notice\n, opens in a new tab\nAccessibility\n, opens in a new tab",
