   "final_url": "https://wildlife.utah.gov/",
   "title": "Hunt, fish & discover - Utah Division of Wildlife Resources",
   "text": "An official website of the state of Utah. Here is how you know\nWildlife Resources\nClose\nAn official website of the state of Utah. Here's how you know:\nOfficial Utah websites use utah.gov in the browser's address bar.\nA Utah.gov website belongs to an official government organization in the state of Utah.\nBe careful when sharing sensitive information.\nShare sensitive information only on secure official Utah.gov websites.\nAn official website\n© State of Utah\nHome\nHunting\nFishing\nDiscover\nLicenses & permits\nNews\nContact us\nSearch\nSportsman permits\nUtah's sportsman hunts\nApplication period now open. Your chance to apply for the hunt of a lifetime!\nAPPLY NOW THROUGH NOV. 10\nwaterfowl\nTime to get on the water.\nBe prepared with the latest details for this year's waterfowl hunts.\nLEARN MORE\nHarvest Reporting\nHunt data helps shape next year’s season\nHarvest reporting is required for all big game hunts and provides crucial insights into Utah's wildlife populations.\nSUBMIT YOUR REPORT\nFISHING\nLicensing, rules and\nyear-round hotspots.\nLearn more\nHUNTING\nLearn about Utah's\ngreat hunting opportunities.\nLearn more\nVIEWING\nFind out more about Utah's\namazing wildlife.\nLearn more\nGet involved with the public process\nNow is the time to share opinions, feedback and ideas on decisions that affect Utah's wildlife.\nTake the survey\nWildlife news\nSee mule deer at upcoming DWR viewing event\nNovember is the perfect time for wildlife watchers and photographers to see mule deer since they are migrating during breeding season and also moving to lower elevations in search of feed. You'll have a great opportunity to see them during an upcoming event!\nRead more\nVisit upcoming exhibit at Hardware Wildlife Education Center to learn about turkeys in Utah\nYou can learn about wild turkeys in Utah — and maybe even see some yourself — by visiting the Hardware Wildlife Education Center in November.\nRead more\nDWR proposes CWMU recommendations, reinstating Pilot Mountain bighorn sheep hunt\nThe Utah Division of Wildlife Resources is proposing to reinstate a bighorn sheep hunt on the Box Elder, Pilot Mountain hunting unit. The DWR is also recommending the renewal of Utah's Cooperative Wildlife Management Units and Landowner Associations for 2027-29 — along with their respective permit allocations — and is seeking the public's feedback on the proposals.\nRead more\nUpcoming events\nList of upcoming events sponsored by the Utah Division of Wildlife Resources\nName Location City Date\nYouth Pheasant Hunt Gordon Creek Wildlife Management Area Helper Saturday, Oct. 31\nBeginner Pheasant Hunt Private property (37.600460, -113.112400) Cedar City Saturday, Nov. 7\nTales and Trails: Story Time for Littles Eccles Wildlife Education Center Farmington Saturday, Nov. 7\nMule Deer Watch Nash Wash Wildlife Management Area Thompson Springs Saturday, Nov. 7\nCentral Region RAC Meeting DWR Central Region Office Springville Tuesday, Nov. 10\nNorthern Region RAC Meeting Weber County Commission Chambers Ogden Thursday, Nov. 12\nBeginner Pheasant Hunt Highway 100, between mile marker 10 and 11 Pahvant Wildlife Management Area Saturday, Nov. 14\nYouth Pheasant Hunt Annabella Wildlife Management Area Annabella Saturday, Nov. 14\nBeginner Adult Pheasant Hunt Pine Canyon Wildlife Management Area Tooele Saturday, Nov. 14\nBeginner Youth Pheasant Hunt Pine Canyon Wildlife Management Area Tooele Saturday, Nov. 14\nSouthern Region RAC Meeting Hunter Conference Center, SUU Cedar City Tuesday, Nov. 17\nSoutheastern Region RAC Meeting John Wesley Powell Museum Green River Wednesday, Nov. 18\nNortheastern Region RAC Meeting DWR Northeastern Region Office Vernal Thursday, Nov. 19\nSee all events\nFollow us:\n1594 W. North Temple\nBox 146301\nSalt Lake City, UT 84114-6301\n801-538-4700\nHelpful links\nReport your harvest\nBuy a hunting/fishing license\nApply for a hunt permit drawing\nGuidebooks\nHunting\nFishing\nAbout us\nPrivacy notice\nConservation programs\nUtah Natural Heritage Program\nUtah Watershed Restoration Initiative\nUtah Wildlife Migration Initiative\nGreat Salt Lake Ecosystem Program\nWildlife news\nNews\nBlog\nPodcast\nEducation centers\nEccles Wildlife Education Center\nHardware Wildlife Education Center\nShooting ranges\nCache Valley Public Shooting Range\nLee Kay Public Shooting Range\nSubscribe\nStay informed about Utah hunting, fishing and wildlife.\nEnter your email address\nSubmit\nInvalid email address.\nEvents\nView the wildlife events calendar\nMobile apps\nUtah Hunting & Fishing mobile app\nRoadkill Reporter\nReport a poacher or wildlife crime\nCall 800-662-3337 or text 847411\nAn official website of the state of Utah\n© 2026 State of Utah\nUtah.gov Home\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nTranslate\nClose\nSearch again\nGive Feedback",
