   "text": "Skip to main content\nReservations\nDiscover Pass\nAbout Us\nFind Parks\nFind Sno-Parks\nFind Activities\nGet Involved\nPasses & Permits\nSearch\nSearch\nHome\nFind Parks\nJackson House State Park Heritage Site\nAlerts\nBurn Ban\nNo fires permitted at any time.\nSee all photos\nJackson House State Park Heritage Site\n4277 Jackson Highway, Winlock, WA, WA 98596\nStep into Washington state history at Jackson House State Park Heritage Site. Relax and take in a picnic at this small day use park after viewing the yesteryear cabin home of a local pioneer.\nAmenities\nPicnic Tables\nAccessible Parking\nParking\nInterpretive Opportunities\nPark features\nField\nRules\nDay-Use Only\nDogs not Allowed\nFires not Allowed\nHorses not Allowed\nSee all other general park rules\nHours\n8:00 a.m. - Dusk year round\nFees\nDiscover pass:\nAnnual Pass: $45\nOne-day Pass: $10\nSee more about fees\nContact\nEmail lewis.clark@parks.wa.gov\nPhone (360) 864-2643\nGet Directions\nGet Discover Pass\nMap & visitor guide\nLocate\nMap\nSatellite\nKeyboard shortcuts\nMap data ©2026 Google\nTerms\nReport a map error\nThings to do at this park\nInterpretive opportunities\nLocated in Winlock, this park was once the homestead of John R. Jackson and his family, the first pioneer settlers north of the Columbia river. Built in 1850, the cabin provides a unique view of early settler life. Preserved through the efforts of women's groups in the 1920s, the cabin was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1974.\nPicnicking\nThe park has picnic tables and grass fields for recreation.\nWinter Schedule\nLearn about seasonal closures and operational changes during the off-season on the Winter Schedule page.\nPark History\nSee all park histories\nMonticello Convention State Park Heritage Site History\nJackson House State Park Heritage Site History\nConnect with us\nContact Us\nCustomer Feedback Form\nNews & Announcements\nSubscribe to Our Email List\nApply for a Job\nWebsite Accessibility\nPublic Records Requests\nReady to get outside?\nMake a Reservation\nBuy a Discover Pass\nGet a Permit\nSee All Alerts and Notifications\nMap and Recreation Guide (PDF)\nFollow us on social media\nFacebook\nInstagram\nYouTube\nLinkedIn\nPrivacy Policy\n© 2006-2024 Washington State Parks and Recreation Commission, WA and its representatives. All rights reserved.",
